# gh-1743: [BUG] Structured compaction timeout (300s budget) aborts session instead of falling back to localTrim

## Description

## Problem Summary
When a background compaction pass (`AutoCompactorFactory.run()`) times out under `CompactionEngine.structured` (hitting the 300s budget watchdog or a network gateway 504 / disconnect), the compaction factory fails fast:

```dart
// lib/src/agent/auto_compactor.dart
if (outcome.timedOut) {
  hooks.onBothRolesFailed(outcome.error!);
  return false;
}
```

Because `false` is returned, the outer continuation funnel (`_maybeOverWindowContinue`) marks compaction as exhausted:
`error: the transcript is still ~X tokens vs a Y-token window — 2 compaction passes did not free it. The task was NOT continued.`
The live session is completely aborted and user workflow is broken.

## Proposed Fix
Instead of immediately aborting with `return false`, apply the existing mechanical `_localTrimFallback()` (which trims down to `keepRecentTokens`, preserves tool pairing integrity, and sets `fallback: 'local-trim'`).

```dart
if (outcome.timedOut) {
  final compactor = build();
  final trimmed = compactor.applyLocalTrimFallback(pass: adapter.passCount + 1);
  if (trimmed) {
    hooks.onDone(adapter.passCount + 1, _requestTokens());
    return true;
  }
  hooks.onBothRolesFailed(outcome.error!);
  return false;
}
```

This rescues the running session, alerts the user with `[context trimmed locally]`, and allows the run to proceed cleanly without stalling or aborting.

